{"id": "1894", "revid": "144844", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=1894", "title": "Atocha", "text": "Atocha is a small mining town of about 10,000 people in Potos\u00ed, Bolivia.\nGet in.\nEither by train from Uyuni/Oruro, or from Tupiza/Villazon, or by bus from Uyuni or Tupiza. The latter options offers much more scenery, well above 4000 m.\nGet around.\nAll walkable.\nSee.\nJust suck in the atmosphere of a genuine Bolivian mining gulch. No tourists here.\nEat.\nMany small eateries.\nSleep.\nSeveral simple inns."}
